# Build context hygiene (T-7-1): never copy local artifacts or secrets into
# the image. node_modules is re-installed per stage (npm ci); docs are not
# needed at runtime; .env* must NEVER reach the image (secrets).
# NOTE (capstone-ui it6 T-6-4): `.github` IS kept in the build context — the
# Dockerfile build stage runs the SAME gate as CI (vitest, incl. the NFR scans
# that read ci.yml and the Dockerfile itself). The monorepo-root `openspec/`
# is OUTSIDE this context: the R-UI-NFR-6 requirement-coverage scan falls back
# to its pinned static ID list inside the image build (mirrors backend
# R-NFR-3). The runtime stage copies ONLY backend/src + backend/scripts +
# ui/dist, so neither .github nor openspec ever reach the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
docs
.git
*.md
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
init
pgdata